NAME
    man - read a manual page

SYNOPSIS
    man [NAME]

DESCRIPTION
    Print the manual page NAME. man reads /usr/share/man/NAME first; if
    there is none it falls back to a short page compiled into the shell,
    which covers the builtins and works before any filesystem is
    reachable. With no NAME it lists the built-in pages.

    Pages are plain text, already formatted, and are printed as they are.
    The section follows the name in references, as in ls(1): 1 for
    commands, 5 for configuration files, 7 for overviews and 8 for the
    administrator's commands.

FILES
    /usr/share/man/   the pages, rebuilt from the verified boot modules at
                      every boot (hier(7))

SEE ALSO
    apropos(1), whatis(1), help(1), horus(7)
